  <purpose>ArchiSurance Case Study - Linked.Archi edition (3.1.0-la.1).

A maintained derivative of &quot;ArchiSurance Case Study, Version 3.1, ArchiMate Model Exchange File Format&quot; by
Henk Jonkers, Iver Band, Dick Quartel and Marc Lankhorst, (c) 2012-2019 The Open Group, published as
document Y194 (https://publications.opengroup.org/y194) under CC BY-SA 3.0
(https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/3.0/).

The ArchiSurance Case Study is a fictitious example developed to illustrate the use of the ArchiMate(R)
modeling language in the context of the TOGAF(R) framework.

Changes by Linked.Archi (see CHANGES.md): empty multilingual placeholders removed; global identifiers
(property &quot;@id&quot;) and architecture state (property &quot;arch:architectureState&quot;) added; metadata added.
Identifiers of elements, relationships and views are unchanged.

This edition is licensed under CC BY-SA 4.0 (https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/).
ArchiMate(R) and TOGAF(R) are registered trademarks of The Open Group.</purpose>
</archimate:model>
